<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucius Licinius Murena (praetor 88 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> Murena was a Roman commander who served under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-mithridatic-war">First Mithridatic War</a> and was left as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. In 83 BCE he attacked Pontus without clear authority, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-mithridatic-war">Second Mithridatic War</a>, and was defeated by Mithridates VI in 82 BCE. Sulla ordered him to stop, but he was nevertheless granted a triumph. His son of the same name was defended by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> in the speech Pro Murena.</p></div>
